eadcrumb"} data-anim={"fade"} data-anim-duration={"800"}><ol className={"breadcrumb"}><li className={"breadcrumb-item"}><a href={"#page=demo-trading-1"}>{"Home"}</a></li><li className={"breadcrumb-item"}><a href={"#page=demo-trading-1-academy"}>{"Academy"}</a></li><li className={"breadcrumb-item"} aria-current={"page"}>{"What Is an ETF?"}</li></ol></nav><h1 id={"tr-page-title"} className={"custom-ph-title max-w-[15ch] font-medium leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.045em] text-(--custom-on-dark) text-balance"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-duration={"1200"}>{"What is an "}<em className={"not-italic text-(--color-primary)"}>{"ETF?"}</em></h1><p className={"max-w-144 mt-7 text-[clamp(1.125rem,1.05rem_+_0.3vw,1.25rem)] leading-[1.55] text-(--custom-on-dark-soft) text-pretty"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"140"}>{"One purchase, hundreds of companies. How exchange-traded funds work, what they cost and where they fit."}</p></div></div></section><section id={"tr-ar-body"} className={"custom-section pt-(--section-space)"} aria-label={"The guide"}><div className={"container"}><article className={"custom-article max-w-[68ch] mx-auto"}><div className={"custom-article-by flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 gap-x-6 pb-8 mb-10 border-b border-b-(--color-border)"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><img className={"w-13 aspect-square object-cover"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/800x800.svg"} alt={""} width={"800"} height={"800"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><p className={"grid leading-[1.35]"}><strong className={"font-semibold text-text"}>{"Sofia Marino"}</strong><span className={"text-[0.9375rem] text-(--custom-meta)"}>{"Senior Analyst · "}<time datetime={"2026-10-02"}>{"2 October 2026"}</time></span></p><p className={"custom-learn-meta grid m-0 leading-[1.35] sm:ms-auto"}><span className={"custom-learn-level text-[0.9375rem] text-(--custom-meta)"}>{"Beginner"}</span><span className={"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[0.9375rem] text-(--custom-meta)"}><i className={"ph ph-book-open"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i>{"6 min read"}</span></p></div><div className={"article-body px-0 text-[1.1875rem] leading-[1.7]"}><p className={"text-[clamp(1.25rem,1.15rem_+_0.4vw,1.4375rem)] leading-[1.6] text-text"}>{"If you’ve ever wanted to own a slice of the whole stock market without picking a single company, an ETF is how most people do it."}</p><p>{"An exchange-traded fund is a basket of investments that trades on a stock exchange like an ordinary share. Buy one unit of a FTSE All-World ETF and you own a tiny piece of around 4,000 companies across 50 countries."}</p><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"}>{"How an ETF works"}</h2><p>{"Most ETFs follow an index: a list of companies chosen by a fixed rule, such as the 100 largest on the London Stock Exchange. The fund buys what’s in the index and changes only when the index does. Nobody is trying to outguess the market, which is why the costs stay low."}</p><p>{"Because they trade on an exchange, ETF prices move throughout the day. You can buy or sell whenever the market is open, in any amount from £1 on Framo Invest."}</p><figure className={"custom-article-chart p-[clamp(1.25rem,1rem_+_1.4vw,2rem)] text-(--custom-on-dark-soft) bg-(--custom-ink) rounded-(--custom-radius-card)"}><p className={"flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-y-2 gap-x-4 mb-6 text-[1rem]"}><strong className={"font-heading text-[1.375rem] font-medium text-(--custom-on-dark)"}>{"A global ETF, ten years"}</strong><span className={"custom-delta-pct custom-delta--up"}>{"+142%"}</span></p><svg className={"custom-chart svg-draw"} data-anim={""} viewBox={"0 0 300 110"} aria-hidden={"true"} focusable={"false"}><defs><linearGradient id={"tr-ar-fill"} x1={"0"} y1={"0"} x2={"0"} y2={"1"}><stop offset={"0"} stopColor={"currentColor"} stopOpacity={".45"}></stop><stop offset={"1"} stopColor={"currentColor"} stopOpacity={"0"}></stop></linearGradient></defs><path className={"custom-chart-area"} fill={"url(#tr-ar-fill)"} d={"M0 100 C14 98 22 92 34 94 C46 96 54 86 66 84 C78 82 86 88 98 80 C110 72 118 76 130 70 C142 64 150 82 162 74 C174 66 182 56 194 52 C206 48 214 58 226 46 C238 34 248 40 260 30 C272 20 286 18 300 10 L300 110 L0 110 Z"}></path><path className={"custom-chart-line"} pathlength={"1"} d={"M0 100 C14 98 22 92 34 94 C46 96 54 86 66 84 C78 82 86 88 98 80 C110 72 118 76 130 70 C142 64 150 82 162 74 C174 66 182 56 194 52 C206 48 214 58 226 46 C238 34 248 40 260 30 C272 20 286 18 300 10"}></path><circle className={"custom-chart-dot"} cx={"296"} cy={"11"} r={"4"}></circle></svg><figcaption>{"Illustrative growth of a world equity index, 2016–2026, with dividends reinvested. Past performance isn’t a reliable indicator of future results."}</figcaption></figure><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"}>{"What it costs"}</h2><p>{"Every fund has a yearly charge, shown as a percentage. For a broad index ETF it’s often between 0.05% and 0.25%. On £1,000 that’s 50p to £2.50 a year, taken from inside the fund rather than from your account."}</p><div className={"py-2 px-4 rounded-(--custom-radius-card) bg-soft"}><table className={"custom-compare w-full tabular-nums text-[1rem]"}><caption className={"sr-only"}>{"ETFs compared with single shares and managed funds"}</caption><thead className={"max-[47.5rem]:hidden"}><tr><th scope={"col"}><span className={"sr-only"}>{"Feature"}</span></th><th scope={"col"}>{"ETF"}</th><th scope={"col"}>{"Single share"}</th><th scope={"col"}>{"Managed fund"}</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Spread of companies"}</th><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"ETF"}>{"Hundreds"}</td><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"Share"}>{"One"}</td><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"Managed fund"}>{"Dozens"}</td></tr><tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Typical yearly cost"}</th><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"ETF"}>{"0.05–0.25%"}</td><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"Share"}>{"None"}</td><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"Managed fund"}>{"0.6–1%"}</td></tr><tr><th scope={"row"}>{"Price updates"}</th><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"ETF"}>{"All day"}</td><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"Share"}>{"All day"}</td><td className={"text-soft"} data-label={"Managed fund"}>{"Once a day"}</td></tr></tbody></table></div><blockquote className={"font-heading border-l-0 pl-0 text-[clamp(1.625rem,1.3rem_+_1vw,2.125rem)] leading-[1.25] tracking-[-0.03em]"}><p className={"leading-[1.2] text-balance"}>{"Owning the haystack is easier than finding the needle."}</p></blockquote><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.035em]"}>{"Where an ETF fits"}</h2><p>{"For many people, one or two broad ETFs make up the core of a portfolio, held for years inside an ISA or a pension. Single shares, if you want them, sit around the edges."}</p><figure><img className={"w-full rounded-(--custom-radius-photo)"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/2000x1333.svg"} alt={"Two tablets and a printed fund factsheet on a table by a window"} width={"2000"} height={"1333"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption>{"Every fund’s factsheet shows what it holds and what it charges."}</figcaption></figure><p>{"ETFs still go down when markets fall. Spreading your money widely smooths the ride, but it doesn’t remove the risk. The longer you can leave it, the more time it has to recover."}</p><div className={"custom-takeaways p-[clamp(1.5rem,1rem_+_1.5vw,2.25rem)] bg-soft rounded-(--custom-radius-card)"}><h2>{"Key takeaways"}</h2><ul className={"custom-checks"} role={"list"}><li>{"An ETF holds many investments in one trade"}</li><li>{"Index ETFs are usually the cheapest way to diversify"}</li><li>{"They rise and fall with the market they track"}</li></ul></div><p className={"custom-risk mt-12"}>{"Capital at risk. This guide is for education only and isn’t a personal recommendation."}</p></div></article></div></section><section id={"tr-ar-related"} className={"custom-section cust